{"id":"deferrals","ord":"a0","title":"Deferrals","desc":"NO DEFERRALS (the human, 2026-08-22): a PR ships everything its item names and everything it spots in touched code; what cannot be done STOPS and ASKS. The Inbox holds only what the human chooses to park. ONE exception: a test found flaky on master that a PR does not own is NOT a deferral — it goes to the Inbox's top-level `flaky tests` ledger, governed by dag-pr-ci's FLAKE POLICY.","created":"2026-08-21T17:25:18-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T10:22:09-04:00"}
{"id":"flaky-tests","ord":"a7","title":"flaky tests — the ledger of tests found flaky on master that no PR owns","desc":"THE LEDGER, not the law: one entry per test file, sightings and dispositions as props on each entry. THE LAW lives in the boot chain — dag-pr-ci's FLAKE POLICY (filed here, dispatched immediately, pi or grok never Opus, one PR when several are open, auto-merge on green). The CI-runs doorbell and the orchestrator's own reading of run logs are the reporting channel (the claude-ci watcher seat retired on the human's ban, 2026-09-01); the orchestrator files what they surface.","created":"2026-08-22T11:51:06-04:00","changed":"2026-09-01T20:18:25-04:00"}
{"id":"awaiting-word","ord":"a8","title":"Awaiting the human's word","desc":"The orchestrator's surfaced-but-unruled ledger, per orch-findings-inbox: each child names a proposal or observation and the word it awaits. Ruled children get their outcome written and are trashed or promoted to a lane.","created":"2026-08-29T11:40:15-04:00"}
{"id":"design-decisions","ord":"a9","title":"design decisions — agents' judgment calls awaiting the human's review","desc":"Choices agents made on their own, for your review — ONLY two kinds reach this queue (your ruling, 2026-08-29 20:15): (1) decisions with USER-FACING impact (what you see, how it behaves, where your data/config lives); (2) creation or non-creation of packages/*. Everything lower-level stays in the PR body's ## Design decisions section for reviewers and never lands here. One parent per PR, one child per qualifying choice, plain words. Reviewed: fine → trash; wrong → a lane to reverse it.","created":"2026-08-29T17:29:00-04:00","changed":"2026-08-29T20:17:08-04:00"}
{"id":"spaces-chat-write-scope","parent":"awaiting-word","ord":"a4","title":"Grant `chat:write` on the kolu Spaces app and reinstall it","todo":true,"desc":"Your live test of #460 (2026-09-02 ~12:37 ET): olai posted, Spaces refused it 403 `missing_permission` — the app JWT lacks `chat:write`. Grok's read: the fix is on the Spaces app, not in olai — grant the scope, reinstall so the grant is approved, and if the JWT is re-issued put it in `$OLAI_SPACES_TOKEN` and restart. The queue keeps the refused digest and retries once the token is accepted; the pill turns from `spaces fault` to `spaces` on the first success. The lane's merge waits on this test passing.","created":"2026-09-02T12:49:11-04:00","custom":{"node":"plugin-spaces-mirror","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/460"}}
{"id":"deferral-2223-group","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a0","title":"kolu#2223's three deferrals — the live bundle","todo":true,"desc":"Named in the PR body's `## Deferrals` by the author (2026-09-02). Each is a scope line the author drew rather than a hole; your ruling on each decides whether #2223 merges with them standing.","created":"2026-09-02T12:58:14-04:00","custom":{"node":"live-bundle","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2223"}}
{"id":"deferral-2223-publisher","parent":"deferral-2223-group","ord":"a0","title":"No `implementRootedSurfacesOnPublisher` constructor","todo":true,"desc":"The shared-publisher constructors exist because kolu's shared publisher carries non-surface channels with the caller's teardown; no rooted-bundle consumer has that problem. A constructor to add when one does, not a flag left open.","created":"2026-09-02T12:58:14-04:00","custom":{"node":"live-bundle","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2223"}}
{"id":"deferral-2223-root-predicate","parent":"deferral-2223-group","ord":"a1","title":"No shared \"is this the root of a bundle?\" predicate","done":"2026-09-02T15:28:54-04:00","desc":"CLOSED BY THE AUTHOR during /be's lens pass (2026-09-02 ~15:27 ET): the \"root must be unprefixed\" law is now one shared predicate across all three doors (connectSurfaces, exposeRootedFaces, implementRootedSurfaces), each keeping its own error class and wording — the third hand-copy this PR added was the failure the cross-citation was betting against. No longer a deferral; nothing for you to rule.","created":"2026-09-02T12:58:14-04:00","changed":"2026-09-02T15:28:54-04:00","custom":{"node":"live-bundle","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2223"}}
{"id":"deferral-2223-extra-groups","parent":"deferral-2223-group","ord":"a2","title":"No `extraGroups`-shaped tags on a live bundle","todo":true,"desc":"A rooted runtime composes the root and its siblings; a host multiplexing hand-written procedures or a keyed map's group still merges them itself with `mergeDisjointGroups`, as kolu-server does today.","created":"2026-09-02T12:58:14-04:00","custom":{"node":"live-bundle","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/kolu/pull/2223"}}
{"id":"deferral-474-group","parent":"deferrals","ord":"a1","title":"olai#474's four deferrals — the server on Cordis","todo":true,"desc":"Named in the PR body's `## Deferrals` by the author (2026-09-02). Two are phase-5 scope lines (browser slots), one is a measured upstream ask the author says is your call to file, one is a cheap guard nothing exercises yet. Your ruling on each decides whether #474 merges with them standing.","created":"2026-09-02T14:57:39-04:00","custom":{"node":"cordis-server","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/474"}}
{"id":"deferral-474-ts-nocheck","parent":"deferral-474-group","ord":"a0","title":"The `@ts-nocheck` stamp stays on the Cordis pin","todo":true,"desc":"Measured: the pinned Cordis is clean under its own tsconfig; under olai's it is ~35 errors, all from five strictness flags (Cordis turns off noImplicitAny, noImplicitThis, strictFunctionTypes; olai adds noUncheckedIndexedAccess, noImplicitOverride), none a bug in Cordis. The five-line upstream ask (\"adopt the two, retire the three\") is drafted in nix/cordis.nix's header — filing it on cordiverse/cordis is yours to decide. The stamp still leaves the pin's exported types computed and olai's call sites checked against them.","created":"2026-09-02T14:57:39-04:00","custom":{"node":"cordis-server","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/474"}}
{"id":"deferral-474-browser-rosters","parent":"deferral-474-group","ord":"a1","title":"The browser's two rosters stay `as const` source files","todo":true,"desc":"WIRES and PLUGINS cannot be data until the tab boots off the roster cell (a browser bundle is built ahead of time; connectSurfaces takes its sibling map at the call), so a third plugin is one row plus two lines. rosters.test.ts holds the three equal. Phase 5 (ctx.slots) retires both.","created":"2026-09-02T14:57:39-04:00","custom":{"node":"cordis-server","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/474"}}
{"id":"deferral-474-redial-unconsumed","parent":"deferral-474-group","ord":"a2","title":"`SurfacesConnection.redial` is not consumed yet","todo":true,"desc":"The client half of the kolu framework ask (#2223) exists; olai has no roster for it to redial until the browser boots off the cell. Phase 5.","created":"2026-09-02T14:57:39-04:00","custom":{"node":"cordis-server","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/474"}}
{"id":"deferral-474-cell-equals","parent":"deferral-474-group","ord":"a3","title":"The `plugins` cell has no `equals`","todo":true,"desc":"The roster republishes on every register and dispose; a re-compose that changed nothing would still send a frame. Nothing re-composes after boot in this phase, so it costs zero frames today; the day a toggle can, it wants one.","created":"2026-09-02T14:57:39-04:00","custom":{"node":"cordis-server","pr-url":"https://github.com/juspay/olai/pull/474"}}
